  "content": {
    "id": "p29-q12-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "12",
    "prompt": "Find the condition for each GP to have a limiting sum, then find that limiting sum.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p29-q12-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$1+(x^2-1)+(x^2-1)^2+\\cdots$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-\\sqrt{2}<x<\\sqrt{2}$ and $x\\ne0$; $S_\\infty=\\dfrac{1}{2-x^2}$.",
          "worked": "$r=x^2-1$. For a limiting sum, $|r|<1$.\n$$\\begin{aligned}-1&<x^2-1<1\\\\0&<x^2<2\\end{aligned}$$\nHence $-\\sqrt{2}<x<\\sqrt{2}$ and $x\\ne0$.\n$$\\begin{aligned}S_\\infty&=\\frac{a}{1-r}\\\\S_\\infty&=\\frac{1}{1-(x^2-1)}\\\\S_\\infty&=\\frac{1}{2-x^2}\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 60
      },
      {
        "id": "p29-q12-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$1+\\dfrac{1}{1+x^2}+\\dfrac{1}{(1+x^2)^2}+\\cdots$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x\\ne0$; $S_\\infty=\\dfrac{1+x^2}{x^2}$.",
          "worked": "$r=\\dfrac{1}{1+x^2}$. For a limiting sum,\n$$\\left|\\frac{1}{1+x^2}\\right|<1.$$\nSince $1+x^2\\ge1$, this holds exactly when $x\\ne0$.\n$$\\begin{aligned}S_\\infty&=\\frac{a}{1-r}\\\\S_\\infty&=\\frac{1}{1-\\frac{1}{1+x^2}}\\\\S_\\infty&=\\frac{1}{\\frac{1+x^2-1}{1+x^2}}\\\\S_\\infty&=\\frac{1}{\\frac{x^2}{1+x^2}}\\\\S_\\infty&=\\frac{1+x^2}{x^2}\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 72
      }
    ]
  },
